\title{OpenCLeaR: OpenCL Easy Accessible from R}
\description{
Provides an easy-to-use interface to OpenCL GPGPU (General-Purpose Computing on Graphics Processing Units) acceleration using a unified C++ abstraction layer via 'Rcpp'. Enables developers to write, compile, and execute hardware-adaptive inline OpenCL C kernels seamlessly from within the R environment. Manages low-level memory transfer, device mapping, and execution queues automatically. Configuration and cross-platform compilation are handled via an integrated 'CMake' infrastructure. The core architecture provides a Just-In-Time (JIT) compilation framework with precision fallbacks and an efficient evaluation-in-place function caching system to eliminate compile-on-invocation overheads.
}
